% The conditions of GDPR Article 33(1) (the notification of a personal data
% breach to the supervisory authority), agent-written in Logical English
% beside a LOMO description of the article (the register probe.le). The
% description gives the duty, its bearer (controllers) and its deadline
% (72 hours after the controller becomes aware of the breach). The text adds
% one condition and one more duty:
%
% - "unless the personal data breach is unlikely to result in a risk to the
%   rights and freedoms of natural persons": the condition of the rule;
% - "Where the notification to the supervisory authority is not made within
%   72 hours, it shall be accompanied by reasons for the delay": a second
%   obligation, for a controller that notifies late.
%
% Regulation (EU) 2016/679: (c) European Union, https://eur-lex.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/oj.
% Copyright Miguel Calejo for the Logical English; Apache License 2.0. Not legal advice.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    the personal data breach of *a controller* is unlikely to result in a risk to the rights and freedoms of natural persons; undefined.
    *a controller* gives the reasons for the delay.

the knowledge base gdpr_article_33_conditions includes these resources:
    probe.

the knowledge base gdpr_article_33_conditions includes:

the text of "http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/art_33/par_1/oj" is at "sources/eli/reg_2016_679_art_33_par_1_oj.txt".

norm gdpr 33 has written conditions.

rule art_33_1 with provenance "http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/art_33/par_1/oj",
        confer "unless the personal data breach is unlikely to result in a risk to the rights and freedoms of natural persons":
the conditions of norm gdpr 33 hold for a controller if
    the controller counts as controllers
    and it is not the case that
        the personal data breach of the controller is unlikely to result in a risk to the rights and freedoms of natural persons.

rule art_33_1_delay with provenance "http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2016/679/art_33/par_1/oj",
        confer "Where the notification to the supervisory authority is not made within 72 hours, it shall be accompanied by reasons for the delay.":
a controller is obliged that the controller gives the reasons for the delay if
    the controller must perform notify the breach by a due date under norm gdpr 33
    and the controller performs notify the breach on a date
    and the date is after the due date.

% ---- cases, with the answers worked out from the text before the run -----

scenario three_breaches is:
    acme is of the type controllers.
    "awareness of a personal data breach" happens to acme on 2026-03-01.
    acme performs notify the breach on 2026-03-05.
    quickco is of the type controllers.
    "awareness of a personal data breach" happens to quickco on 2026-05-10.
    quickco performs notify the breach on 2026-05-12.
    safeco is of the type controllers.
    "awareness of a personal data breach" happens to safeco on 2026-06-01.
    the personal data breach of safeco is unlikely to result in a risk to the rights and freedoms of natural persons.
    deadlines expects answers ["acme must perform notify the breach by 2026-03-04 under norm gdpr 33", "quickco must perform notify the breach by 2026-05-13 under norm gdpr 33"].
    met expects answers ["quickco met notify the breach under norm gdpr 33"].
    reasons expects answers ["acme is obliged that acme gives the reasons for the delay"].

query deadlines is:
    which party must perform notify the breach by which date under norm gdpr 33.

query met is:
    which party met which action under which rule.

query reasons is:
    which party is obliged that which party gives the reasons for the delay.
